{"ts": 1791257850.0616739, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: You\u2019re looking for the distinction between the two evaluation styles:\n\n- **pass@k** = at least one of k tries succeeds\n- **pass^k** = all k tries succeed\n\nFor the build, the point is usually to argue about **reliability**. So if your system needs to work every time when deployed, pass^k is the stricter and more relevant measure. pass@k is more like \u201ccan it succeed sometimes if we try enough times?\u201d\n\nA simple way to write the eval section:\n1. Say what you measured.\n2. Say why that metric matches the goal.\n3. Mention any proxy/direct measure tradeoff.\n\nIf you want, send me your draft eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help tighten it up.\n[t=0] student: hm ok\n[t=4] agent: Got it \u2014 if you\u2019re still stuck, paste the exact eval section you\u2019ve written so far and I\u2019ll edit it with you. If you haven\u2019t written it yet, here\u2019s a fill-in template:\n\n\u201cOverall, we evaluate our system using ____. This metric is appropriate because our goal is ____. We also note the difference between a proxy measure and the direct outcome we care about: ____ is a proxy, while ____ is the more direct measure of success.\u201d\n\nIf you send me 2\u20133 sentences from your draft, I\u2019ll turn them into a clean final version.\n[t=4] student: sure\n[t=6] agent: Great \u2014 paste the eval paragraph here and I\u2019ll help revise it line by line. If it\u2019s short, I can also draft a clean version for you to adapt.\n[t=6] student: sure\n[t=7] agent: No worries \u2014 if you haven\u2019t pasted it yet, send me the eval paragraph now. I\u2019ll rewrite it into a polished version you can use, and I\u2019ll keep it focused on pass@k vs pass^k and the proxy/direct measure point.\n[t=7] student: hm ok\n[t=8] agent: Let\u2019s keep this moving. Send me the exact eval paragraph you have so far, even if it\u2019s rough or incomplete. If you prefer, you can also send bullet points and I\u2019ll turn them into a paragraph for you.", "t": 9, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.40784989287081264, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791257851.093121, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I\u2019m happy to help, but I still need the actual eval text from your draft. Please paste the paragraph or even just 2\u20133 bullet points, and I\u2019ll rewrite it for you right away. If it helps, include:\n- what you evaluated\n- what metric you used\n- why that metric fits the build\n- whether it\u2019s a proxy or direct measure", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=9 messages 1m", "t": 10, "activity": [{"t": 9, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.35535796159308425}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.35784989287081265, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791257853.113297, "type": "step", "step": 18, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the answer you can use for the eval section:\n\n\u201cWe evaluate the system using pass^k, meaning all k runs must succeed, because the goal is reliable performance rather than occasional success. pass@k would be a looser metric since it only requires one successful run out of k. We also distinguish proxy and direct measures: a quick test or quiz score is a proxy, while the real outcome we care about is whether the system actually performs well in the target task over time.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can make this shorter or more specific to your exact build.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can we stop for a bit\n[activity] t=10 messages 1m", "t": 11, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.3610667584845955}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.30784989287081266, "reliance": 0.5740148929158049, "persistence": 0.4420657842665555, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
